### US-01-R1-F01 — Anonymous draft reads on Strapi's port (published-only middleware bypass)

The middleware strips `status`, `publicationFilter`, `hasPublishedVersion` and `publicationState`
only when `ctx.path.startsWith('/api/') && !ctx.get('authorization')`. Neither condition matches
how Strapi authenticates or routes:

1. **Header presence is not authentication.** Strapi's content-API strategies (API token,
   users-permissions JWT) only consider `Bearer <token>`. Any other `Authorization` value is
   ignored, the request falls back to the **public role**, and the publication parameters are
   kept. The comment at lines 8-11 ("an invalid one is refused with 401") is true only for
   `Bearer <something>`.
2. **The path check is case-sensitive, Strapi's router is not.** `/API/form-fields` reaches the
   same `find` route without passing the `/api/` test.

Evidence, fresh `mci-review` stack (seeded draft `email` field in CO and CL), Strapi's own port:

```
GET /api/form-fields?status=draft&filters[key][$eq]=email                         -> 200, data: []      (correct)
  + Authorization: Bearer garbage                                                  -> 401                 (correct)
  + Authorization: foo | Basic Zm9vOmJhcg== | Bearer | x                            -> 200, 2 drafts (ids 9, 28, publishedAt null)
GET /API/form-fields?status=draft&filters[key][$eq]=email   (no header at all)     -> 200, 2 drafts
GET /Api/form-fields?status=draft&...                       (no header at all)     -> 200, 2 drafts
GET /api/countries?status=draft  + Authorization: foo                              -> 200, draft countries
```

Through the proxy (`:8080`) the same requests are refused: `Authorization` → 400, and `/API/…`
falls through to `index.html`. But ADR-0002 states that drafts stay unreadable "even when
someone calls Strapi's port directly", and port 1337 is published on every interface
(`docker-compose.yml:6`). The `status=draft` filter is the only control left on that port, and it
is open. This breaks BR-06 ("no anonymous caller can read them, not even by asking the content
API for `status=draft`") and the first AC-28 scenario. The leaked data is low-sensitivity, but the
AC and the ADR rule are explicit. Severity: **blocker** (security rule, AC broken).

Expected: an anonymous request (no **valid** API token) never receives non-published content,
whatever its headers or path casing. Suggested direction (optional): decide on the
authentication result rather than the raw header, for example by forcing `status` after Strapi
has authenticated the request (route-level middleware or policy on the content API that checks
the authenticated strategy), or by rejecting unknown `Authorization` schemes. Also compare the
path case-insensitively. Strapi has its own `strapi::query` parsing, so re-check
`publicationState` and future parameters (ADR-0002 *Strongest argument against*).

### US-01-R1-F02 — AC-28 tests miss the anonymous variants

`us-01-security.spec.ts` sends `status=draft` (and three other publication parameters) with no
`Authorization` header and lower-case paths only. All 32 e2e tests pass while F01 is open, so the
test would not catch a regression either. ADR-0002 says the draft rule "is guarded by an
automated anonymous request for the seeded draft field, re-run on every Strapi upgrade", so that
guard must cover the bypasses found above: at least one non-Bearer `Authorization` value, an
empty `Bearer`, and a non-lower-case `/API/` path, on Strapi's port, for `form-fields` (and
ideally `countries`). This is a test-engineer task, separate from the F01 fix commit (CLAUDE.md
§10).

### US-01-R1-F03 — Unparseable number input is wiped from the screen

`onNumberInput` sets the model to `''` whenever `validity.badInput` is true. Signal Forms then
writes `''` back to the control, so the text the person sees is erased while they type. Probe in
Chromium on CL "Año", typed key by key:

| Typed | Input shows | Stored raw value |
|---|---|---|
| `2015.5` | `2015.5` | `"2015.5"` |
| `1e` | *(empty)* | `""` |
| `-5` | `-5` | `"-5"` |
| `1e5` | `5` | `"5"` |

import type { FieldConfig, FieldType, SelectOption, ValidationRule } from './field-config.model';

const KEY = /^[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]*$/;
const TYPES: readonly FieldType[] = ['text', 'number', 'select', 'date', 'checkbox'];
export const FALLBACK_MESSAGE = 'Revisa este campo.';

/** Rule kinds and the field type each one applies to (spec 7.1). */
const APPLIES_TO: Record<string, FieldType> = {
  minLength: 'text',
  maxLength: 'text',
  pattern: 'text',
  rutCheckDigit: 'text',
  min: 'number',
  max: 'number',
  yearRange: 'number',
  minAge: 'date',
};

type Rec = Record<string, unknown>;
const isRec = (v: unknown): v is Rec => typeof v === 'object' && v !== null && !Array.isArray(v);
const isStr = (v: unknown): v is string => typeof v === 'string';
const isFieldType = (v: unknown): v is FieldType => TYPES.some((t) => t === v);
const isNonEmpty = (v: unknown): v is string => isStr(v) && v.trim() !== '';

/** A finite number, also accepted when Strapi sends it as numeric text. */
function num(v: unknown): number | null {
  if (typeof v === 'number') return Number.isFinite(v) ? v : null;
  if (isStr(v) && /^-?\d+(\.\d+)?$/.test(v.trim())) return Number(v);
  return null;
}
const nonNegativeInt = (v: unknown): number | null => {
  const n = num(v);
  return n !== null && Number.isInteger(n) && n >= 0 ? n : null;
};

function parseRule(raw: unknown, type: FieldType): ValidationRule | null {
  if (!isRec(raw) || !isStr(raw['kind']) || APPLIES_TO[raw['kind']] !== type) return null;
  const message = isNonEmpty(raw['message']) ? raw['message'] : undefined;
  switch (raw['kind']) {
    case 'minLength':
    case 'maxLength': {
      const value = nonNegativeInt(raw['value']);
      return value === null ? null : { kind: raw['kind'], value, message };
    }
    case 'min':
    case 'max': {
      const value = num(raw['value']);
      return value === null ? null : { kind: raw['kind'], value, message };
    }
    case 'pattern': {
      if (!isNonEmpty(raw['value'])) return null;
      try {
        new RegExp(`^(?:${raw['value']})$`);
      } catch {
        return null;
      }
      return { kind: 'pattern', value: raw['value'], message };
    }
    case 'minAge': {
      const years = nonNegativeInt(raw['years']);
      return years === null || years === 0 ? null : { kind: 'minAge', years, message };
    }
    case 'yearRange': {
      const maxYearsOld = nonNegativeInt(raw['maxYearsOld']);
      const maxYearsAhead = nonNegativeInt(raw['maxYearsAhead']);
      return maxYearsOld === null || maxYearsAhead === null ? null : { kind: 'yearRange', maxYearsOld, maxYearsAhead, message };
    }
    case 'rutCheckDigit':
      return { kind: 'rutCheckDigit', message };
    default:
      return null;
  }
}

function parseOptions(raw: unknown): SelectOption[] | null {
  if (!Array.isArray(raw) || raw.length === 0) return null;
  const options: SelectOption[] = [];
  for (const o of raw) {
    if (!isRec(o) || !isStr(o['value']) || !isNonEmpty(o['label'])) return null;
    const sortOrder = num(o['sortOrder']);
    if (sortOrder === null) return null;
    options.push({ value: o['value'], label: o['label'], sortOrder });
  }
  if (new Set(options.map((o) => o.value)).size !== options.length) return null;
  return options.sort((a, b) => a.sortOrder - b.sortOrder || a.value.localeCompare(b.value));
}

/** Parses one item; returns the config or the reason it was dropped. */
function parseItem(raw: unknown): FieldConfig | string {
  if (!isRec(raw)) return 'not an object';
  const key = raw['key'];
  if (!isStr(key) || !KEY.test(key)) return 'invalid key';
  const fieldType = raw['type'];
  if (!isFieldType(fieldType)) return 'unknown type';
  if (!isNonEmpty(raw['label'])) return 'empty label';
  if (typeof raw['isRequired'] !== 'boolean') return 'invalid isRequired';
  const sortOrder = num(raw['sortOrder']);
  if (sortOrder === null) return 'invalid sortOrder';

  const rawRules = Array.isArray(raw['rules']) ? raw['rules'] : [];
  const rules: ValidationRule[] = [];
  for (const r of rawRules) {
    const parsed = parseRule(r, fieldType);
    if (parsed === null) return 'malformed rule';
    rules.push(parsed);
  }

  let options: SelectOption[] | undefined;
  if (fieldType === 'select') {
    const parsed = parseOptions(raw['options']);
    if (parsed === null) return 'invalid options';
    options = parsed;
  }

  let errorMessage = FALLBACK_MESSAGE;
  if (isNonEmpty(raw['errorMessage'])) {
    errorMessage = raw['errorMessage'];
  } else {
    console.warn(`field config: "${key}" has no errorMessage, using the fallback message`);
  }

  return {
    key,
    type: fieldType,
    label: raw['label'],
    helpText: isNonEmpty(raw['helpText']) ? raw['helpText'] : undefined,
    placeholder: isNonEmpty(raw['placeholder']) ? raw['placeholder'] : undefined,
    isRequired: raw['isRequired'],
    sortOrder,
    errorMessage,
    requiredMessage: isNonEmpty(raw['requiredMessage']) ? raw['requiredMessage'] : undefined,
    options,
    rules,
  };
}

/**
 * Boundary validation of the Strapi response (spec 7.1, US-01-AC-14): malformed fields are dropped
 * with a `console.warn` that names the key and the problem, never labels, texts or values.
 * Returns the valid fields sorted by `sortOrder`, ties broken by key; for a repeated key the
 * first one in that order wins.
 */
export function parseFieldConfigs(response: unknown): FieldConfig[] {
  const data = isRec(response) ? response['data'] : null;
  if (!Array.isArray(data)) {
    console.warn('field config: unexpected response shape');
    return [];
  }
  const parsed: FieldConfig[] = [];
  for (const raw of data) {
    const result = parseItem(raw);
    if (typeof result === 'string') {
      const key = isRec(raw) && isStr(raw['key']) ? raw['key'] : '(unreadable)';
      console.warn(`field config: "${key}" dropped (${result})`);
    } else {
      parsed.push(result);
    }
  }
  parsed.sort((a, b) => a.sortOrder - b.sortOrder || a.key.localeCompare(b.key));
  const seen = new Set<string>();
  return parsed.filter((f) => {
    if (seen.has(f.key)) {
      console.warn(`field config: "${f.key}" dropped (duplicated key)`);
      return false;
    }
    seen.add(f.key);
    return true;
  });
}
import type { Country } from './country.model';

const isRec = (v: unknown): v is Record<string, unknown> => typeof v === 'object' && v !== null && !Array.isArray(v);

/**
 * Boundary validation of the country list (ADR-0001): `code` is an upper-case ISO alpha-2 code,
 * `name` is non-empty, `currencyCode` is an ISO 4217 alpha-3 code. Invalid entries are dropped
 * with a `console.warn` that never carries content. Sorted by `sortOrder`.
 */
export function parseCountries(response: unknown): Country[] {
  const data = isRec(response) ? response['data'] : null;
  if (!Array.isArray(data)) {
    console.warn('country list: unexpected response shape');
    return [];
  }
  const countries: Country[] = [];
  for (const raw of data) {
    if (
      isRec(raw) &&
      typeof raw['code'] === 'string' &&
      /^[A-Z]{2}$/.test(raw['code']) &&
      typeof raw['name'] === 'string' &&
      raw['name'].trim() !== '' &&
      typeof raw['currencyCode'] === 'string' &&
      /^[A-Z]{3}$/.test(raw['currencyCode']) &&
      typeof raw['locale'] === 'string' &&
      typeof raw['sortOrder'] === 'number'
    ) {
      countries.push({
        code: raw['code'],
        name: raw['name'],
        currencyCode: raw['currencyCode'],
        locale: raw['locale'],
        sortOrder: raw['sortOrder'],
      });
    } else {
      console.warn('country list: an entry was dropped (invalid code, name, currency or locale)');
    }
  }
  return countries.sort((a, b) => a.sortOrder - b.sortOrder || a.code.localeCompare(b.code));
}
import { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';
import { Injectable, inject } from '@angular/core';
import { Observable, map } from 'rxjs';
import { parseCountries } from '../shared/country';
import type { Country } from '../shared/country.model';
import { contentGet } from './content-request';

@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class CountryContentApi {
  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);

  /** The published countries, sorted by `sortOrder`, with only the attributes the app uses. */
  list(): Observable<Country[]> {
    return contentGet(this.http, 'countries', {
      sort: 'sortOrder:asc',
      'fields[0]': 'code',
      'fields[1]': 'name',
      'fields[2]': 'currencyCode',
      'fields[3]': 'locale',
      'fields[4]': 'sortOrder',
      'pagination[pageSize]': '100',
    }).pipe(map(parseCountries));
  }
}
# Stage 1: build the Angular application (production configuration).
FROM node:24-alpine AS build
WORKDIR /app
ENV NG_CLI_ANALYTICS=false CI=1
COPY package.json package-lock.json ./
RUN npm ci
COPY . .
RUN npx ng build --configuration production

# Stage 2: serve it with nginx and proxy /api to Strapi (ADR-0002).
FROM nginx:1.29-alpine
# Processed by the image's envsubst at container start into /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf.
COPY nginx/default.conf.template /etc/nginx/templates/default.conf.template
COPY --from=build /app/dist/frontend/browser /usr/share/nginx/html
# Address of Strapi inside the compose network, without a trailing slash. Override at run time.
ENV STRAPI_UPSTREAM=http://strapi:1337
EXPOSE 80
