877:### 7.5 Wire shapes (Strapi 5 REST) and mapping to the logical shape (v0.4)
878-
879-Added in v0.4 after code review round 1 (US-01-R1-F04, US-01-R1-F05; human decisions of
880-2026-11-21; physical model in ADR-0006, which amends ADR-0001's physical model). The developers
881-implement the backend to return exactly these shapes, and the front-end boundary parser
882-(`field-config.ts`, `country.ts`) maps them to the logical shapes. The test-engineer derives the
883-parser fixtures from them.
884-
885-#### 7.5.1 Validation rule (`form.validation-rule` component, inside a form field's `rules`)
886-
887-Every rule on the wire carries **all** of the attributes below. The attributes its kind does not
888-use are `null`. Strapi adds the component `id`, which the parser ignores.
889-
890-| Wire attribute | JSON type on the wire | Used by kind(s) | Editor input (Strapi admin) |
891-|---|---|---|---|
892-| `kind` | string, one of `minLength`, `maxLength`, `min`, `max`, `pattern`, `minAge`, `yearRange`, `rutCheckDigit` | all | enumeration (required) |
893-| `value` | number or `null` | `minLength`, `maxLength`, `min`, `max` | numeric input |
894-| `pattern` | string or `null` | `pattern` | plain text input: the regex is typed as is (`^\d+$`), with no JSON quoting or doubled backslashes |
895-| `years` | integer or `null` | `minAge` | integer input |
896-| `maxYearsOld` | integer or `null` | `yearRange` | integer input |
897-| `maxYearsAhead` | integer or `null` | `yearRange` | integer input |
898-| `message` | string or `null` | all (optional override, US-01-Q-04) | text input |
899-
900-The Strapi attribute types (for example `integer` versus `decimal` for `value`, `string` versus
901-`text` for `pattern`) and their schema-level minimums are fixed in ADR-0006; whatever they are,
902-the JSON types above hold. Every current use of `value` is an integer (lengths, and bounds of
903-integer-only `number` fields, US-01-Q-12).
904-
905-Examples (wire), as returned inside `data[i].rules` of `GET /api/form-fields`:
906-
907-```json
908-{ "id": 41, "kind": "pattern",   "value": null, "pattern": "^[A-Za-z]{3}[0-9]{3}$", "years": null, "maxYearsOld": null, "maxYearsAhead": null, "message": null }
909-{ "id": 42, "kind": "minLength", "value": 3,    "pattern": null, "years": null, "maxYearsOld": null, "maxYearsAhead": null, "message": "Ingresa tu nombre completo (entre 3 y 80 caracteres)." }
910-{ "id": 43, "kind": "minAge",    "value": null, "pattern": null, "years": 18,   "maxYearsOld": null, "maxYearsAhead": null, "message": null }
911-{ "id": 44, "kind": "yearRange", "value": null, "pattern": null, "years": null, "maxYearsOld": 20,   "maxYearsAhead": 1,    "message": null }
912-{ "id": 45, "kind": "rutCheckDigit", "value": null, "pattern": null, "years": null, "maxYearsOld": null, "maxYearsAhead": null, "message": null }
913-```
914-
915-(The values are illustrative; the seed values are in [seed-fields.md](seed-fields.md).)
916-
917-Mapping wire → logical `ValidationRule` (§7.1), applied per rule by the boundary parser:
918-
919-| Wire `kind` | Parameter read from the wire | Valid when | Logical rule produced |
920-|---|---|---|---|
921-| `minLength`, `maxLength` | `value` | a JSON number, integer, ≥ 0 | `{ kind, value }` |
922-| `min`, `max` | `value` | a JSON number, finite | `{ kind, value }` |
923-| `pattern` | `pattern` | a non-empty JSON string that compiles as an ECMAScript regex with no flags | `{ kind: 'pattern', value: <pattern> }` |
924-| `minAge` | `years` | a JSON number, integer, > 0 | `{ kind: 'minAge', years }` |
925-| `yearRange` | `maxYearsOld`, `maxYearsAhead` | both JSON numbers, integers, ≥ 0 | `{ kind: 'yearRange', maxYearsOld, maxYearsAhead }` |
926-| `rutCheckDigit` | none | always | `{ kind: 'rutCheckDigit' }` |
927-
928-Rules of the mapping:
929-
930-1. The logical `ValidationRule` of §7.1 is unchanged: the logical `pattern` rule keeps its
931-   regex in `value`, so validators and their tests do not change. Only the parser reads a
932-   different wire attribute for `pattern`.
933-2. `message`: a non-empty string becomes the logical `message`; `null`, an empty or a blank
934-   string means "no override".
935-3. Attributes the kind does not use are **ignored**, whatever their value (an editor who
936-   changes a rule's kind may leave a stale value behind). They are `null` in the seed.
937-4. A rule is **malformed** when its `kind` is unknown, does not apply to the field's type
938-   (§7.1), or the parameter its kind reads is missing, `null`, of the wrong JSON type (numeric
939-   text such as `"3"` is a wrong type) or out of range. A malformed rule makes its field
940-   malformed: the field is dropped with a `console.warn` naming the field key and the problem,
941-   with no user data (US-01-Q-18, AC-14).
942-
943-#### 7.5.2 Country (`country` collection type)
944-
945-The API exposes the stored attribute name **`localeTag`**, with no renaming in the backend (no
946-custom controller mapping `fields`, `sort` or `filters`; human decision on US-01-R1-F05). It can
947-therefore be selected, sorted and filtered as `localeTag` like any other attribute. The front end
import {
  Component,
  Injector,
  OnInit,
  effect,
  inject,
  input,
  signal,
  untracked,
  type WritableSignal,
} from '@angular/core';
import { FieldTree, FormField, FormRoot, REQUIRED, form, metadata, validate } from '@angular/forms/signals';
import { Router } from '@angular/router';
import { CLOCK } from '../../core/clock';
import { QuoteStore } from '../../core/quote-store';
import type { FieldConfig, RawValues } from '../../shared/field-config.model';
import { validateField } from '../../shared/field-validators';
import { hydrate } from '../../shared/field-values';

/**
 * The step 1 form (ADR-0004): Signal Forms over the shared validation core. The editing model is
 * `Record<string, string | boolean>` (never null); each field has exactly one `validate()` that
 * calls the pure `validateField`. Built once per instance, hydrated from the wizard state; a
 * different configuration means a new instance (the page recreates it).
 */
@Component({
  selector: 'app-quote-form',
  imports: [FormField, FormRoot],
  templateUrl: './quote-form.html',
  styleUrl: './quote-form.css',
})
export class QuoteForm implements OnInit {
  readonly configs = input.required<FieldConfig[]>();
  readonly countryCode = input.required<string>();

  private readonly injector = inject(Injector);
  private readonly clock = inject(CLOCK);
  private readonly quote = inject(QuoteStore);
  private readonly router = inject(Router);

  protected form!: FieldTree<RawValues>;
  private model!: WritableSignal<RawValues>;

  ngOnInit(): void {
    const configs = this.configs();
    const model = signal<RawValues>(hydrate(configs, this.quote.values()));
    this.model = model;
    this.form = form(
      model,
      (root) => {
        for (const config of configs) {
          validate(root[config.key], ({ value }) => {
            const message = validateField(config, value(), this.clock());
            return message ? { kind: 'custom', message } : undefined;
          });
        }
      },
      {
        injector: this.injector,
        submission: {
          action: async () => {
            if (this.quote.completeStep1(configs) !== null) {
              await this.router.navigate(['/', this.countryCode().toLowerCase(), 'planes']);
            }
            return undefined;
          },
          onInvalid: (root) => {
            const first = configs.find((config) => root[config.key]().invalid());
            if (first) root[first.key]().focusBoundControl();
          },
        },
      },
    );

    // The raw editing values are written to the wizard state on every change (ADR-0003).
    let synced: RawValues = { ...model() };
    effect(
      () => {
        const current = model();
        untracked(() => {
          for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(current)) {
            if (synced[key] !== value) this.quote.setValue(key, value);
          }
          synced = { ...current };
        });
      },
      { injector: this.injector },
    );
  }

  /** The two narrowing accessors of ADR-0004: the only casts, selected by the field type. */
  protected text(key: string): FieldTree<string> {
    return this.form[key] as unknown as FieldTree<string>;
  }
  protected flag(key: string): FieldTree<boolean> {
    return this.form[key] as unknown as FieldTree<boolean>;
  }

  /**
   * A number input the browser cannot parse (`1e`) reads back as '' and Signal Forms keeps the
   * previous text in the model. That stale text would later be written back into the DOM by the
   * deferred control binding, replacing what the user is typing, so the model follows the
   * input: unparseable counts as empty (spec AC-09).
   */
  protected onNumberInput(key: string, event: Event): void {
    const input = event.target;
    if (input instanceof HTMLInputElement && input.validity.badInput && this.model()[key] !== '') {
      this.model.update((values) => ({ ...values, [key]: '' }));
    }
  }

  /**
   * The message to show (spec AC-09): input the browser cannot parse never reaches the model (it
   * keeps the last parseable text) but Signal Forms reports a parse error without a message, so
   * that case is evaluated as an empty value: `requiredMessage ?? errorMessage`.
   */
  protected errorOf(config: FieldConfig): string | null {
    const state = this.form[config.key]();
    if (!state.touched() || !state.invalid()) return null;
    const errors = state.errors();
    if (errors.some((error) => error.kind === 'parse')) {
      return validateField(config, '', this.clock()) ?? config.errorMessage;
    }
    return errors[0]?.message ?? null;
  }

  protected describedBy(config: FieldConfig, error: string | null): string | null {
    const ids = [
      config.helpText ? `${config.key}-help` : '',
      error ? `${config.key}-error` : '',
    ].filter(Boolean);
    return ids.length > 0 ? ids.join(' ') : null;
  }
}
